     "freshness_acknowledgement_chain_repair_20260731": "This session's acknowledgement-writer REPLACED the acknowledgement list instead of appending to it, collapsing a 9-link chain to 3 and destroying 7 committed arc_executable_world_model.py drift records (restored here: 9 committed links + 1 new = 10). No path lost coverage, which is exactly why it was invisible to a path-level check -- each destroyed link recorded a DISTINCT drift event with its own sha256_was -> sha256_now and reason, and the chain is what lets a reader see when each drift was accepted and why. Recorded rather than silently fixed, per the never-prune rule this violated."
